        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "59f9e18f-430f-5d37-aee6-c05c03b16a25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Miller, Randy Travis\n- Songs: \"King of the Road\", \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\"\n- Albums: I Told You So: The Ultimate Hits of Randy Travis, Around the Bend\n- Topics: country music, Nashville sound\n\nFacts:\n- Roger Miller was born on January 2, 1936, and he was an American singer-songwriter, musician, and actor.\n- Roger Miller was best known for honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs during the mid-1960s Nashville sound era.\n- Roger Miller wrote and originally recorded the song \"King of the Road\" in November 1964.\n- Roger Miller's most recognized tunes included the chart-topping country and pop hits \"King of the Road\", \"Dang Me\", and \"England Swings\".\n- Roger Miller released the song \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\" in 1965.\n- Randy Travis's album I Told You So: The Ultimate Hits of Randy Travis includes his cover of Roger Miller's \"King of the Road\" and two tracks from Around the Bend.\n- Roger Miller died on October 25, 1992.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
